  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the correct grammatical construction of $P⇔Q$ is the following:\n\n$\\,$ A triangle is right **if and only if** it has two complementary angles.",
